RISC3D test kit 27 (prototype, 14 November 2026)
================================================

Kit 26's results: only software was right, so none of those five
changes is the cause. But the pictures show a pattern: each texture
looks like one row of it stretched across the surface. The HUD text
and dials (textures without mipmaps) are always right; the car, trees
and grass (textures with mipmaps) are wrong.

This kit's rol-3d (0.15) checks the textures themselves on the GPU.
After drawing frame 240 it reads every texture level back from the GPU
and compares it with what TORCS uploaded, and it draws two test cards:
every texture in a grid, with mipmaps (cardmip) and from the full-size
level only (cardbase).

Steps
-----
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing kit 26.
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.15-1_arm64.deb
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/replay /riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-477.r3d 240
    It runs twice: GPU, then software.

